{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_015d9311a3c7d0f494195148097418c2e38216355fd50d2d9df6823d17301dd4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"maruakshay/miii-cli@0a712d9f2d68 snapshot 5960cfd3fa980381","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_20078a2a89a60912b7dd4be41acc93082874dfdde0baf3a11b43743bae72f171","slc_2e231b27b3d6463bdccc1802a46572beb639dc0af226634f16d7a2b63342e734"],"source_ids":["src_e60d147462be5bbdbd24840007b0c4ef"],"text":"The tool requires Node 18 or newer and Ollama, and is distributed as the npm package miii-agent.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0d46e7893c507521421fae6db105bdf2cb65ba526029dfe820d8e16d8d61f972","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"maruakshay/miii-cli@0a712d9f2d68 snapshot 5960cfd3fa980381","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a2976525d5df4e1ba4d4dafde8ab9edcefe84d33a36ae5ea71471d610f235258"],"source_ids":["src_e60d147462be5bbdbd24840007b0c4ef"],"text":"The agent repairs malformed tool calls from small models and sizes its prompt to the model's context window, and a MIII.md file in the repo is read every turn to teach project conventions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_47e0a3693cdf4b5803d63499e9b3b036fdc0155079da584746be22a3bae2f439","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"maruakshay/miii-cli@0a712d9f2d68 snapshot 5960cfd3fa980381","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8dbdef07cfa68946763aee42e376bcb4a5a947101dc58a95bc669a782f926ba9"],"source_ids":["src_e60d147462be5bbdbd24840007b0c4ef"],"text":"File tools reject ../ traversal and absolute paths outside the workspace, while run_bash is not path-confined and is bounded only by the permission prompt.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5bb8339a525f232b1789181de9300440f42109a223e51726b4ac71a3ab0c1c0b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"maruakshay/miii-cli@0a712d9f2d68 snapshot 5960cfd3fa980381","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0877a319ec502300b1801533697e6cec536f9a1c8c443da57547505e42da2871","slc_114fa58744d5efacb4912de97b79c0742c5e2b2f817cb626620c048c7f329091"],"source_ids":["src_e60d147462be5bbdbd24840007b0c4ef"],"text":"Saved approval rules live in .miii/permissions.json per project (with an optional global ~/.miii/permissions.json), and sessions can be saved and resumed via /new and /sessions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_71db020bbd3913059e2e39478ff3b91b20476bf96f50e9f47f41f691d3345d68","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"maruakshay/miii-cli@0a712d9f2d68 snapshot 5960cfd3fa980381","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a2976525d5df4e1ba4d4dafde8ab9edcefe84d33a36ae5ea71471d610f235258","slc_e850565fa15815bac5233dfa0f23dd68b47340d0d9d552b891c61830ed875a2b"],"source_ids":["src_e60d147462be5bbdbd24840007b0c4ef"],"text":"The product includes `miii doctor`, which grades the user's installed local models on real engineering tasks to check whether they can drive an agent.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8507b87c0fbe5a1bea32b5da0b1b64a9e902ea5fc29da90240584449cc439107","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"maruakshay/miii-cli@0a712d9f2d68 snapshot 5960cfd3fa980381","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1bba34190f31104a573ef5b754c919b5074cb54a8798bb9e7f63ae2cc5cf60db","slc_26656bc0489e966d05c11ef31b5665bffd920770fd75fa26fc828dd47fc738b0","slc_c16fc178c93a468f60a279224468e67e6dbf83eb8b9d4737b15bf4e0d9f828b2"],"source_ids":["src_e60d147462be5bbdbd24840007b0c4ef"],"text":"Four permission modes cycle via shift+tab: normal, plan (read-only), auto-accept edits, and bypass; 'always' approvals save exact commands plus globs that never span command boundaries or match destructive programs.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8788b4ff918329fb1db305305d5e066e956a8b27f70667dc5de361a421a333ca","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"maruakshay/miii-cli@0a712d9f2d68 snapshot 5960cfd3fa980381","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1953ed8a854b93e1ef9cec05c872dbb397220d54d61f1b819ec777e0c16f922d","slc_379f94a31c98d3a5a613c3fab90c59b4fa46da46a16f7571ea23f131ccae81a5"],"source_ids":["src_e60d147462be5bbdbd24840007b0c4ef"],"text":"Tool output over ~10K bytes is spilled to ~/.miii/output/<id>.txt with a head/tail preview inline; the model pages through the file with ranged reads and spill files are garbage-collected after 24 hours.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c42c0120ad210182b0a99d55f402b56119ddd26b3132858890aa43b95a634c2b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"maruakshay/miii-cli@0a712d9f2d68 snapshot 5960cfd3fa980381","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_364996c4b9203c1c8803dc8c317b7c309edb806e19295f57a75737f755dd8f50","slc_78e351abb0a138e557d44de52aba59af288ea4449a25f90491d7eee43f7320a2","slc_dd66cc78f8719adef439ace212b16e28cab200fbfed786181d53f1633ae6206c"],"source_ids":["src_e60d147462be5bbdbd24840007b0c4ef"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors clone the repo, run npm install && npm run dev, and use npm run build, npm run typecheck, npm test, and npm run eval (a regression gate powering miii doctor); npm run build && npm link runs the working tree as the global miii.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_cc53973488d3af3a7d5ef5139cd7fa5f1176027f60bcd24e79fc937dd8d0fdcd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"maruakshay/miii-cli@0a712d9f2d68 snapshot 5960cfd3fa980381","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0877a319ec502300b1801533697e6cec536f9a1c8c443da57547505e42da2871","slc_b2fd64c793a47c10133f54ddd52d1ea5acbe3d6e691c46a73846f2e7704f834f"],"source_ids":["src_e60d147462be5bbdbd24840007b0c4ef"],"text":"The CLI exposes slash commands (/plan, /permissions, /models, /sessions, /compact, /copy, /clear, /exit), a command palette on '/', and keyboard shortcuts such as Shift+Tab for permission modes and Ctrl+V for image paste.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d864208656c219dba9bf6098875b0b273af5369e56538de528e888b4d34ff782","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"maruakshay/miii-cli@0a712d9f2d68 snapshot 5960cfd3fa980381","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9a4b8388f3fad1adaab01151d0b92ee041aa70dfb81dc4bbc944c35f7c4fb3e5","slc_a70c4d4a8f0b7a16634a84ad738c8352a7e8cd4fe7d64d06f0be1bcf44574896"],"source_ids":["src_e60d147462be5bbdbd24840007b0c4ef"],"text":"miii is a local terminal AI coding agent that runs against Ollama with no API keys or cloud, positioned as an offline alternative to cloud coding assistants.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_eaaa84747daa921a19272b09fbbaf34be6318692c9dbbee2d887a8b860f04ebc","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"maruakshay/miii-cli@0a712d9f2d68 snapshot 5960cfd3fa980381","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_98d612333e94521616486f6f671986ad9f7fc479d16bd0aa3bb3866a91be9c80","slc_d7d459fc2cd83c929c9ab0b550e256c062a3f12643d3e7d5429df0073421da08"],"source_ids":["src_e60d147462be5bbdbd24840007b0c4ef"],"text":"Besides Ollama, miii can talk to any OpenAI-compatible local server such as llama.cpp, LM Studio, or vLLM, selected via config providers or --provider at launch.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f27c42c8ce85e6ab374d2c3e35cb02b98de5e69d2a04290925a6703d95af998a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"maruakshay/miii-cli@0a712d9f2d68 snapshot 5960cfd3fa980381","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_766bf7ec399d5775a1ce1d3f711770884e351f110081461bddaad0ac80f831ea"],"source_ids":["src_e60d147462be5bbdbd24840007b0c4ef"],"text":"Built-in agent tools include read_file, write_file, edit_file, glob, grep, run_bash, and write_todos for tracking multi-step work.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f44125e1bc73a93e9e2034bd71bdcb86376fe7b3ccc3b5ccf612c2ab1f5f3f82","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"maruakshay/miii-cli@0a712d9f2d68 snapshot 5960cfd3fa980381","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_741a7ca6131782634c5d9f47b0155761d19bdd86241303184b72cfc3b2531aa3","slc_833a3aa82ca81f6067a698ec98096c2227740509f3c6c582ee9078e719af98e2","slc_9f5bd83783f6b1e0f7d31d15318f66693b727e068cb0133e40c4b3fdc68718f0"],"source_ids":["src_e60d147462be5bbdbd24840007b0c4ef"],"text":"Custom slash commands are Markdown files in .miii/commands/ (project scope) or ~/.miii/commands/ (personal), supporting $ARGUMENTS and $1-$9 substitution, with project commands shadowing personal ones but never built-ins.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_675772a436bd41d7bb645899d5f29408"}
